# Unified-diff encoding, not source whitespace: every context line of a patch
# gets a leading space, so tab-indented C context reads as space-before-tab and
# a blank context line is a lone space. Waived for these two patch files and only for
# those two checks; added (`+`) lines are verified separately by
# `make check-patch-whitespace`. Everything else keeps the default checks.
patches/libraop-media-write-callback.patch whitespace=-space-before-tab,-blank-at-eol
patches/libraop-raop-client-thread-races.patch whitespace=-space-before-tab,-blank-at-eol
